# Dataset
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# Compressed Commit E: data/manifests/ holds generated CSVs
# (merge_candidates.csv, merge_manual_labels.csv, merge_manifest.csv)
# that must stay gitignored during development (large/regeneratable),
# but the directory itself is tracked via .gitkeep so the expected
# layout is documented in the repo.
!data/manifests/
data/manifests/*
!data/manifests/.gitkeep

# Phase 2 Stage B-1.5: the maneuver_id -> scene_key -> split assignment
# is a frozen research decision (controller/FSM threshold tuning must
# never see validation-split scenes), not a regeneratable dataset
# artifact -- tracked deliberately, unlike the other manifests above.
!data/manifests/phase2_dataset_split.csv

# Phase 2 Stage C-1: the dataset-difficulty descriptor + interaction
# -tag table is deterministically reproducible from tracked code
# (scripts/build_phase2_dataset_descriptors.py +
# scripts/apply_phase2_difficulty_tags.py) and the frozen
# configs/phase2_difficulty.yaml thresholds, but is tracked directly
# per Stage C Section 14 so the exact frozen values used by later
# analysis/evaluation are visible without rerunning the pipeline.
!data/manifests/phase2_dataset_difficulty.csv

# MERGE Decision Dataset v2 freeze record: a frozen research decision
# (version/git SHA/filter config hash/candidate counts/known
# limitations), not a regeneratable bulk manifest -- tracked directly
# so the exact frozen state is visible without rerunning the freeze
# pipeline, matching the phase2_dataset_split.csv precedent above.
# Git requires every ancestor directory to be explicitly un-ignored for
# a nested file negation to take effect (data/manifests/* alone blocks
# it even with a file-level "!" rule); re-excluding the directory's own
# contents right after keeps every OTHER file under data/manifests/v2/
# (raw evidence JSONL, GIF-adjacent CSVs, etc.) still hard-ignored.
!data/manifests/v2
data/manifests/v2/*
!data/manifests/v2/MERGE_DECISION_DATASET_V2_FREEZE.json

# Generated outputs
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc

# Virtual / Environment
.env
.venv/
venv/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Logs
*.log

# W&B local run artifacts (docs/ppo/PPO_PLAN.md SS8) -- offline-run
# directories are local run logs/binaries, not source; see
# docs/ppo/SMOKE_TRAINING_REPORT.md SS12 for the referenced run paths.
wandb/
